From 75cb965428f9be75e5b70da6a121dda5f27e7d32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gnanaprakash Elumalai <gelumala@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:21:13 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] prplMesh: address CURE controller safety findings

Problem:

Controller paths can dereference failed database lookups, TLV
allocations, message parses, or optional payloads. Failed BML requests
can also leave published promises and output pointers active or expose
uninitialized scan data.

Root cause:

Runtime objects and decoded message elements were assumed to be
available, while several BML early-return paths did not clear request
state and scan results were copied before confirming asynchronous
success.

Fix:

Validate lookups, allocations, parsed responses, and optional data
before use. Initialize scan outputs, clear published BML state on every
failure path, and copy results only after successful request completion.

Signed-off-by: Gnanaprakash Elumalai <gelumala@qti.qualcomm.com>
